 "result_text": "`checkout_github_prs()` now prints a warning and returns without error when no PRs match `--all`, `--mine` or `--by`. I haven't run the tests or tried it against a real repository.\n\nThe changes are in `git_machete/client.py`:\n- **Warning instead of error:** `__get_valid_pull_requests` used to raise for \"no open PRs in the repo\", \"current user has no open PRs\" and \"user X has no open PRs\". Each case now warns and returns an empty list.\n- **Early return:** `checkout_github_prs` returns straight away when that list is empty. It therefore skips the fetch, the definition-file updates and the final checkout.\n\nExplicit PR numbers behave as before. If you pass numbers and none of them exist, it still raises. I read \"criteria\" in the issue as the `--all`, `--mine` and `--by` filters, so I left that case alone. If you want it to warn instead, it's the two `raise` calls in the `if prs_list:` branch.",
